WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.550
Step three: fix the problem.

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.825
From your seven thirty fix, lay a new course line to the mark.

3
00:00:07.075 --> 00:00:10.550
You start from where you are, not from where you meant to be.

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:16.450
Draw a current diagram, with the current setting one six zero at one point six knots.

5
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:22.425
From it, read the course to steer that holds you on the new line, and your speed made good along it.

6
00:00:22.675 --> 00:00:29.525
Convert that course to compass for the helmsman, using the variation, and the deviation for the new heading.

7
00:00:29.775 --> 00:00:32.200
Last, the new arrival time.

8
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:36.450
Measure the distance still to run, and divide it by a speed.

9
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.300
Which speed?

10
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.175
Your speed made good.

11
00:00:41.425 --> 00:00:43.275
Not your boat speed.

12
00:00:43.525 --> 00:00:47.600
That’s the last trap in the problem, and now you won’t fall into it.
